"Gravity-Defying McMurtry Spéirling Is First Car to Drive Upside Down From Idle", "url": "https://mobile.guideautoweb.com/en/articles/78226/gravity-defying-mcmurtry-speirling-is-first-car-to-drive-upside-down-from-idle"}, {"title": "Engineering news", "url": "https://www.imeche.org/news/news-article/how-and-why-mcmurtry-made-a-car-that-can-drive-upside-down"}, {"title": "McMurtry Spirling drives upside down from stationary", "url": "https://the-mia.com/news/698581/McMurtry-Spirling-drives-upside-down-from-stationary.htm"}, {"title": "McMurtry Spirling can now drive upside down", "url": "https://www.completecar.ie/car-news/article/14041/McMurtry-Spirling-can-now-drive-upside-down"}, {"title": "www.carscoops.com", "url": "https://www.carscoops.com/?p=3188676"}, {"title": "GLOBALE |  MENA", "url": "https://evlife.world/it/?p=29635"}]}, "The driver was **Thomas Yates**, McMurtry Automotive's co-founder and managing director, and the sources agree on that point. They differ on the date and duration.\n\n- **Driver:** With co-founder and managing director Thomas Yates behind the wheel, the technology demonstration took place at McMurtry's headquarters in Gloucestershire, England.\n- **Date:** Wikipedia and Top Gear give 11 April 2025 (Published: 11 Apr 2025). IMechE says the world-first demo on 10 April.\n- **Duration:** Wikipedia says the car was driven upside down for five seconds. IMechE says it slowly edged forwards for just seven seconds.\n- **Setup:** The car was driven up a ramp onto a platform that rotated it, and it was held in place by its fan system. Top Gear describes this as a special purpose-built platform… which then rotated to fully invert the hypercar. Its downforce-on-demand system kept it attached to the platform, and that system doesn't need speed to operate.\n- **Downforce:** IMechE reports the fan system can generate 2,000kg of downforce – without any forward movement."], "durationSeconds": 6.569334875000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Ewxnf1gp2znHfEZacutPUv", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
